13  finally getting an under display touch  id sensor so it would match up  perfectly and what's really interesting  is that a few months ago  a new patent granted to apple showed a  touch id sensor built into the side  button  which actually looks very similar to the  new touch id power button on the ipad  air 4.  so that might make a lot of sense for  apple to do and apparently  they're working on an under display  camera which would actually be  really cool but here is by far the most  exciting report that we got  in terms of the apple watch series 7.  ming chi kuo a fairly reliable leaker  said that we should expect a brand new  form factor  for this year's watch and if we take a  look at where apple has been going with  the recent  design changes it's pretty obvious that  apple's going to try to give it a more  flat design  like in this very nice looking render  and making it even better  quo mentioned that apple would be coming  out with new innovative health  management functions  with the new series seven and the most  rumored one  we're all expecting is of course blood  glucose monitoring  this has been rumored for years but we  haven't actually seen it because of how  difficult it is  to check blood sugar levels without the  traditional method of pricking your  finger  but recently et news reported that this  feature  will actually be debuting on the apple  watch series 7  potentially using an optical sensor to  do it however  a lot of people are skeptical because no  one really has this type of technology  right now  so apple would have to invent some  totally new tech to make it happen  and a couple of months ago mark german  from bloomberg  said that apple may launch a new rugged  apple watch model  for extreme sports as soon as this year  apparently apple employees are  internally calling it the explorer  edition  which would have the same functionality  as a standard apple watch  but with extra impact resistance and  protection  and then going further he mentioned that  apple is working on  new swim tracking features for the apple  watch as well but the absolute banger  leak that recently  came out a few weeks ago was from john  prosser  who apparently got his hands on images  of a brand new apple watch design  with flat sides and a totally redesigned  speaker grill layout  i've gotta say that these renders by  ian's elbow look absolutely amazing  and they look perfectly in line with  what you'd expect from apple  looking similar to the new iphone and  the imac design  with those flat sides and according to  john source  apple has been working on experimental  colors for the apple watch  including a new green so what if apple  is thinking of giving the watch  the same colors as maybe the ipad air  which would be a pretty cool marketing  move from apple so as you guys can see  based on all of those very exciting  leaks and rumors  we've all got some pretty massive  expectations  for the apple watch series seven but  sorry guys  this brand new report from bloomberg's  mark german is about to burst your  bubble  first off i want to mention that mark is  one of the most reliable apple leakers  out there  with basically 90 accuracy which is even  more impressive  when you consider the fact that his  rumor count is now over 400 rumors  and while everyone including myself  thought that the m1x macbook pros were  coming at wwdc  he was saying the complete opposite and  he was right  so let's get into his new report mark  says that the new apple watch series 7  is coming with a few improvements  namely a faster processor improved  wireless connectivity  and an updated screen apple is  apparently testing a model with thinner  display borders and a new lamination  technique  that brings the display closer to the  front cover  he even said that the new watch is  likely to be slightly thicker overall  but not in a way that's noticeable to  the user now this detail is very  interesting because it makes it seem  like micro led  is finally coming but with all of the  supply chip shortages going around  i honestly don't think it's ready or  else mark would have specifically  mentioned it  and if micro led was actually coming in  this year's apple watch series 7  it would have likely made it thinner and  lighter like we heard from the previous  reports  instead of making it thicker like mark  is saying in this brand new report  and yes the new faster processor is  exciting but to be honest  the current s6 chip in the series 6 is  20 faster than the s5 chip  but in day to day use you can't really  notice any difference because both chips  are already fast enough to run watch os  just fine so i don't even think we  really need  a much faster chip and as far as  wireless connectivity improvements  apple could potentially bring 5g to the  apple watch  but if you think about it 4g is already  draining battery life  very quickly and as we all know 5g is a  huge  battery hog and in reality you don't  really need super fast 5g speeds on an  apple watch  so maybe apple's just gonna be upgrading  the bluetooth spec  to the new 5.2 version which is gonna  make it more future proof  for the next few years of iphones but  here is where mark's new report gets  very depressing apparently apple had  previously aimed to put a body  temperature sensor in this year's model  but it's likely getting delayed until  next year  and on top of that the long-awaited  blood sugar sensor is  unlikely to be ready for a commercial  launch for several more  years and making it even worse mark says  that the new rugged extreme sports  edition  won't arrive until next year at the  earliest  so all of those exciting features are  getting delayed  so i guess in reality the best hope for  the apple watch series 7  is the new redesign that jon prosser  showed off  a few weeks ago but if apple was  planning the redesign for this year's  watch  then mark german would have likely  mentioned it since he's usually the  first to mention apple product redesigns  and on top of that even john prosser  himself  thinks that the redesign he showed off  could be delayed until next year  just listen to this clip from his video  in fact everything goes by code names  behind the scenes so this source wasn't  even  able to confidently say that this was  apple watch series 7.  for all we know this could also be  series 8. so yeah  john is saying that there's a chance  that the redesign is not coming until  the series 8  which would actually make sense and  match up to mark german's new report  which is basically making the series 7  look quite  boring missing out on the features that  people actually wanted  and that's why i don't think it's worth  waiting for it and my other reason for  not waiting  is because the current apple watch  series 6 is on sale  right now on amazon being a full 70  off for both the 40 millimeter size and  the 44  millimeter size if you use the links  below so the main question that each  person has to answer for themselves  is this is it worth waiting another  three months  for the series 7 which could potentially  be a very boring update  or should you just buy the current  series 6 for a killer deal  right now and enjoy using it throughout  this entire  busy summer that's all up to you to  decide but if you enjoyed this video  go ahead and click the circle about to  subscribe for more videos like this one  definitely check out one of those two  right there thanks for watching and  we'll see you in  the next video

